plt.ylabel('Number of Skills', fontsize=12)
plt.xticks(rotation=45)
plt.tight_layout()

# Save the plot
plt.savefig('Skills1.png', bbox_inches='tight')
plt.close()

# Indicate success
print('Image generated successfully.')
``` 

The code uses the `matplotlib` and `seaborn` libraries to create and save a bar graph, visualizing the counts of different skill groups in demand. The image is saved as "Skills1.png" and is centered with proper layout adjustments to ensure clarity and prevent any clipping or unnecessary whitespace.

The visualization should be engaging and suitable for display on a frontend. If the code runs successfully, it will produce the success message 'Image generated successfully.' If any issues arise during the execution, it will indicate that 'Visualization can't be generated.'
